WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.070
- I have to ask this

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:03.960
because I didn't know that
you had like a bagpipe phase.

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:04.890
- Oh my God.

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.348
Our family's got,
- [Kelly] Which is awesome.

00:00:06.348 --> 00:00:08.510
- our family has Scottish roots.

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:09.343
- [Kelly] Okay,
- And I always-

00:00:09.343 --> 00:00:10.176
- But a lot of people have Scottish roots

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:11.152
that don't play the bagpipe.
- Yes.

00:00:11.152 --> 00:00:11.985
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:11.985 --> 00:00:14.220
But I really love the sound of bagpipes.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:15.053
- [Kelly] It's beautiful.

00:00:15.053 --> 00:00:19.300
- And I got it on a consignment, you know?

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.568
Thrifts, or whatever you call that,

00:00:20.568 --> 00:00:23.552
the sheet when you get used
stuff, you know, the newspaper?

00:00:23.552 --> 00:00:25.610
Remember those?
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:26.570
- I do.
- [Bonnie] And it was for sale

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:27.403
and I bought 'em.

00:00:27.403 --> 00:00:30.039
And I asked in my college paper,

00:00:30.039 --> 00:00:32.040
I advertised in the Want ads

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.365
for anybody that knew how to blow.

00:00:34.365 --> 00:00:38.687
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:00:38.687 --> 00:00:40.818
And then it said like this,
"Bagpipes." underneath,

00:00:40.818 --> 00:00:42.270
and that was my ad.

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:43.103
- Oh my God.

00:00:43.103 --> 00:00:44.315
I was like, what kind of
results happened after?

00:00:44.315 --> 00:00:45.837
- And then I get, I said,

00:00:45.837 --> 00:00:49.340
"Know how to blow bagpipes,
freshman wants to learn."

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.530
But my-
- Freshman wants to learn.

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:55.530
- And my housemates at my dorm

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:56.650
they wouldn't let me learn.

00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:57.892
'Cause it just sounds like
someone's being strangled.

00:00:57.892 --> 00:00:59.630
- Well it's so loud.

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:00.470
- [Bonnie] Yeah. Oh, it's terrible.

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:01.520
- Yeah.
- [Bonnie] Really bad.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:02.353
- But it is beautiful.

00:01:02.353 --> 00:01:03.860
- And I was like passing out from,

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:05.500
I didn't have the air to
blow through that thing.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:06.490
- [Kelly] To sustain.
- [Both] Yeah.

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:07.560
- Yeah, it seems hard.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:08.393
- [Bonnie] I like it,
- To hold it all and

00:01:08.393 --> 00:01:09.568
- [Bonnie] but too hard.

00:01:09.568 --> 00:01:10.401
I know it was too hard for me.

00:01:10.401 --> 00:01:11.234
I'm glad I stuck with the guitar.

00:01:11.234 --> 00:01:12.670
- I think we all are, yeah.
(audience clapping)

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:13.734
- Thank you.

00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:15.534
- I think that was a solid decision.

